4\\,$ | $\\,0.711\\,$ | $\\,1.064\\,$ |\n| $5$ | $\\,0.412\\,$ | $\\,0.554\\,$ | $\\,0.831\\,$ | $\\,1.145\\,$ | $\\,1.610\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X>x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>x) & =1-P(X\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.005 \\\\  & =0.995\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{χ}^{2}(4),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=4.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $\\,0.207\\,$ | $\\,0.297\\,$ | $\\,0.484\\,$ | $\\,0.711\\,$ | $\\,1.064\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X>0.207)=0.995.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=0.207.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ccb2367b-54fc-50aa-8684-3aa2a710859d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ccb2367b-54fc-50aa-8684-3aa2a710859d" :answer-field/id #uuid "ccb2367b-54fc-50aa-8684-3aa2a710859d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d6fc4ad5-887a-55cb-91ae-8042270e76d2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-760efcf4-e371-5ee5-8095-2afc058abad2" "answer-d6fc4ad5-887a-55cb-91ae-8042270e76d2" "answer-487a0cb4-3b3c-53b1-ad75-19be1635b445" "answer-801fb805-5abf-578a-bed5-8eed93de26a8" "answer-3b9b65f2-32b1-5306-a674-1a8cce394049"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-760efcf4-e371-5ee5-8095-2afc058abad2" :answer/id #uuid "760efcf4-e371-5ee5-8095-2afc058abad2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.072" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6fc4ad5-887a-55cb-91ae-8042270e76d2" :answer/id #uuid "d6fc4ad5-887a-55cb-91ae-8042270e76d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.207" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-487a0cb4-3b3c-53b1-ad75-19be1635b445" :answer/id #uuid "487a0cb4-3b3c-53b1-ad75-19be1635b445" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.352" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-801fb805-5abf-578a-bed5-8eed93de26a8" :answer/id #uuid "801fb805-5abf-578a-bed5-8eed93de26a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.412" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b9b65f2-32b1-5306-a674-1a8cce394049" :answer/id #uuid "3b9b65f2-32b1-5306-a674-1a8cce394049" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.711" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161926 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5c65221c-bb24-5314-9566-2deac5724c52"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5c65221c-bb24-5314-9566-2deac5724c52" :question/id #uuid "5c65221c-bb24-5314-9566-2deac5724c52" :question/math-academy-id "q-252041" :question/problem "Let the random variable $Y$ be defined as\n\n$$\nY={Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{50}^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${Z}_{i}∼N(0,1)$ for $1\\le i\\le 50.$ Find the value $y$ such that $P(Y\\le y)=0.85.$\n\n*Hint: The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.010$ | $0.050$ | $0.100$ | $0.150$ | $0.200$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $48$ | $\\,73.683\\,$ | $\\,65.171\\,$ | $\\,60.907\\,$ | $\\,58.135\\,$ | $\\,55.993\\,$ |\n| $49$ | $\\,74.919\\,$ | $\\,66.339\\,$ | $\\,62.038\\,$ | $\\,59.241\\,$ | $\\,57.079\\,$ |\n| $50$ | $\\,76.154\\,$ | $\\,67.505\\,$ | $\\,63.167\\,$ | $\\,60.346\\,$ | $\\,58.164\\,$ |\n\nThe value of $y$ that satisfies $P(Y\\le y)=0.85$ is $y=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "If ${Z}_{i}∼N(0,1)$ for $1\\le i\\le k$ are independent normal random variables, then the sum\n\n$$\n{Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{k}^{2}\n$$\n\nfollows a ${χ}^{2}(k)$ distribution with $k$ degrees of freedom.\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\nY={Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{50}^{2}∼{χ}^{2}(50).\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the given probability in the form $P(Y\\ge y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le y) & =1-P(Y\\ge y) \\\\ 0.85 & =1-P(Y\\ge y) \\\\ P(Y\\ge y) & =0.15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we wish to find the value $y$ such that $P(Y\\ge y)=0.15$ This can be found from the given table:\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.010$ | $0.050$ | $0.100$ | $0.150$ | $0.200$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $48$ | $\\,73.683\\,$ | $\\,65.171\\,$ | $\\,60.907\\,$ | $\\,58.135\\,$ | $\\,55.993\\,$ |\n| $49$ | $\\,74.919\\,$ | $\\,66.339\\,$ | $\\,62.038\\,$ | $\\,59.241\\,$ | $\\,57.079\\,$ |\n| $50$ | $\\,76.154\\,$ | $\\,67.505\\,$ | $\\,63.167\\,$ | $\\,60.346\\,$ | $\\,58.164\\,$ |\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y\\ge 60.346)=0.15\n$$\n\nwhich means\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le 60.346)=0.85.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=60.346.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-346fec95-da88-5e3b-8992-afee68fefadc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-346fec95-da88-5e3b-8992-afee68fefadc" :answer-field/id #uuid "346fec95-da88-5e3b-8992-afee68fefadc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5731441f-975d-55af-aa2c-666c2201d3f5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5731441f-975d-55af-aa2c-666c2201d3f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5731441f-975d-55af-aa2c-666c2201d3f5" :answer/id #uuid "5731441f-975d-55af-aa2c-666c2201d3f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60.346" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-f53cd9ea-6553-5efb-a7b8-f3c13f72a44b" :activity/id #uuid "f53cd9ea-6553-5efb-a7b8-f3c13f72a44b" :activity/title "The Chi-Square Distribution" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050266 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-14676990-70ab-5297-b2c1-9c3014d28e45" "step-e4cf7475-8f17-5f68-9d68-3550e7152e3a" "step-dd8b0eaf-0121-540c-b3dc-4528fcf15e64" "step-8743147f-7556-5e5e-a7d0-2c7a8c3a230d" "step-d35e5081-77a0-59a9-80ae-7f654b2e8813"] :activity/first-step "step-14676990-70ab-5297-b2c1-9c3014d28e45" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-14676990-70ab-5297-b2c1-9c3014d28e45" :step/id #uuid "14676990-70ab-5297-b2c1-9c3014d28e45" :step/content "question-9a27da7c-7cd5-581c-8018-40a7c4e9ff5d" :step/next "step-e4cf7475-8f17-5f68-9d68-3550e7152e3a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e4cf7475-8f17-5f68-9d68-3550e7152e3a" :step/id #uuid "e4cf7475-8f17-5f68-9d68-3550e7152e3a" :step/content "question-b4dc7492-4019-5d98-a361-736ee5b48968" :step/next "step-dd8b0eaf-0121-540c-b3dc-4528fcf15e64" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-dd8b0eaf-0121-540c-b3dc-4528fcf15e64" :step/id #uuid "dd8b0eaf-0121-540c-b3dc-4528fcf15e64" :step/content "question-ed8bb07d-ed88-5d7c-a376-b5b20e72fc61" :step/next "step-8743147f-7556-5e5e-a7d0-2c7a8c3a230d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8743147f-7556-5e5e-a7d0-2c7a8c3a230d" :step/id #uuid "8743147f-7556-5e5e-a7d0-2c7a8c3a230d" :step/content "question-c1169ae0-dbcc-5afc-b27c-5d1844b9830b" :step/next "step-d35e5081-77a0-59a9-80ae-7f654b2e8813" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d35e5081-77a0-59a9-80ae-7f654b2e8813" :step/id #uuid "d35e5081-77a0-59a9-80ae-7f654b2e8813" :step/content "question-5c65221c-bb24-5314-9566-2deac5724c52" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096708 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f789e17e-9222-50f7-90e6-3a489f3b51f3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f789e17e-9222-50f7-90e6-3a489f3b51f3" :question/id #uuid "f789e17e-9222-50f7-90e6-3a489f3b51f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-79303" :question/problem "![](images/84/84fa3bc1d70144b0fd2d1865e784ed1cee9d8b83633547f2e62be1a30e4242aa.png)\n\nWhat is the $y$-intercept of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(2,-5)$ and passes through the point $(-2,3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(2,-5)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}=4p(y+5).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-2,3),$ we substitute $x=-2$ and $y=3$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2-2)^{2} & =4p(3+5) \\\\ 16 & =4p(8) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =2(y+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-2)^{2} & =2(y+5) \\\\ 4 & =2(y+5) \\\\ y & =2-5 \\\\ y & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b313a6a7-5aef-5eef-9fdc-9a3f6384635e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b313a6a7-5aef-5eef-9fdc-9a3f6384635e" :answer-field/id #uuid "b313a6a7-5aef-5eef-9fdc-9a3f6384635e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9f61033c-bec0-5a9b-aaf9-ae37b563257c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c192c3f6-fee4-5de2-baf8-b83ae6c0b752" "answer-9f61033c-bec0-5a9b-aaf9-ae37b563257c" "answer-b078e7a8-a8b1-5f0a-8d3b-7817778a5e09" "answer-e6374016-52a5-5c7e-89fb-b178fcb7aab0" "answer-a4366df5-83ab-5bf1-a218-b427953b47ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c192c3f6-fee4-5de2-baf8-b83ae6c0b752" :answer/id #uuid "c192c3f6-fee4-5de2-baf8-b83ae6c0b752" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f61033c-bec0-5a9b-aaf9-ae37b563257c" :answer/id #uuid "9f61033c-bec0-5a9b-aaf9-ae37b563257c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b078e7a8-a8b1-5f0a-8d3b-7817778a5e09" :answer/id #uuid "b078e7a8-a8b1-5f0a-8d3b-7817778a5e09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6374016-52a5-5c7e-89fb-b178fcb7aab0" :answer/id #uuid "e6374016-52a5-5c7e-89fb-b178fcb7aab0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4366df5-83ab-5bf1-a218-b427953b47ad" :answer/id #uuid "a4366df5-83ab-5bf1-a218-b427953b47ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096706 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f822983e-1d14-50b6-989d-68e7f1c76860" "question-fdc8ed74-44a5-549d-abf7-39e6c995f550" "question-735e4f99-1ffc-57e4-b137-966d99c9aba8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f822983e-1d14-50b6-989d-68e7f1c76860" :question/id #uuid "f822983e-1d14-50b6-989d-68e7f1c76860" :question/math-academy-id "q-240667" :question/problem "![](images/ac/ac9ee9825678ad3ba815204c39ac2fe4ea85972cc60458251fcc9e9fdb4ba0f7.png)\n\n**From left to right**, the **exact values** of the $x$-intercepts of the parabola shown above are{{field-1}}and{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-1,3)$ and passes through the point $(-2,\\frac{5}{2}).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-1,3)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2} & =4p(y-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-2,\\frac{5}{2}),$ we substitute $x=-2$ and $y=\\frac{5}{2}$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2+1)^{2} & =4p(\\frac{5}{2}-3) \\\\ (-1)^{2} & =4p(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ 1 & =-2p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2} & =-2(y-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2} & =-2(0-3) \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =6 \\\\ x+1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{6} \\\\ x & =-1\\pm \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are $-1-\\sqrt{6}$ and $-1+\\sqrt{6}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b06a318c-820e-5ff0-97ca-8c71655f9348" "answer-field-34e53936-bbb9-5fb0-9b7e-e35958cdf4b9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b06a318c-820e-5ff0-97ca-8c71655f9348" :answer-field/id #uuid "b06a318c-820e-5ff0-97ca-8c71655f9348" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-46bda047-ac5b-540d-b339-64ed2abef508" :answer-field/choices ["answer-46bda047-ac5b-540d-b339-64ed2abef508"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46bda047-ac5b-540d-b339-64ed2abef508" :answer/id #uuid "46bda047-ac5b-540d-b339-64ed2abef508" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1-\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-34e53936-bbb9-5fb0-9b7e-e35958cdf4b9" :answer-field/id #uuid "34e53936-bbb9-5fb0-9b7e-e35958cdf4b9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-168bd404-2959-5371-bc5c-7fbba3473aa1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-168bd404-2959-5371-bc5c-7fbba3473aa1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-168bd404-2959-5371-bc5c-7fbba3473aa1" :answer/id #uuid "168bd404-2959-5371-bc5c-7fbba3473aa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1+\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fdc8ed74-44a5-549d-abf7-39e6c995f550" :question/id #uuid "fdc8ed74-44a5-549d-abf7-39e6c995f550" :question/math-academy-id "q-251773" :question/problem "![](images/75/7515041ccdceb8d13e4e718bda12af7535cfbb4a37b0180b04f88a08db4947b2.png)\n\n**From left to right**, the values of the $x$-intercepts of the parabola shown above are{{field-1}}\nand \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(3,-1)$ and passes through the point $(0,\\frac{5}{4}).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(3,-1)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =4p(y+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(0,\\frac{5}{4}),$ we substitute $x=0$ and $y=\\frac{5}{4}$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-3)^{2} & =4p(\\frac{5}{4}+1) \\\\ 9 & =4p(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ p & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =4(y+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =4(0+1) \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm 2+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are $1$  and $5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6377b71b-3301-54ad-85e4-81211618a817" "answer-field-d11afbdb-9351-5d55-af3d-0ebc6b7799e3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6377b71b-3301-54ad-85e4-81211618a817" :answer-field/id #uuid "6377b71b-3301-54ad-85e4-81211618a817" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0d6f31a7-12c7-533a-a616-32df997a304f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0d6f31a7-12c7-533a-a616-32df997a304f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d6f31a7-12c7-533a-a616-32df997a304f" :answer/id #uuid "0d6f31a7-12c7-533a-a616-32df997a304f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d11afbdb-9351-5d55-af3d-0ebc6b7799e3" :answer-field/id #uuid "d11afbdb-9351-5d55-af3d-0ebc6b7799e3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1d14f365-3431-51a2-85f1-fb6aa4f3083e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1d14f365-3431-51a2-85f1-fb6aa4f3083e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d14f365-3431-51a2-85f1-fb6aa4f3083e" :answer/id #uuid "1d14f365-3431-51a2-85f1-fb6aa4f3083e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-735e4f99-1ffc-57e4-b137-966d99c9aba8" :question/id #uuid "735e4f99-1ffc-57e4-b137-966d99c9aba8" :question/math-academy-id "q-251783" :question/problem "![](images/7a/7ac752bbc51ea08ba8723fa0aba111d3f302cc149db8762208ae18ed31be02d1.png)\n\n**From left to right**, the values of the $x$-intercepts of the parabola shown above are{{field-1}}\nand \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(1,-4)$ and passes through the point $(0,-3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(1,-4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2} & =4p(y+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(0,-3),$ we substitute $x=0$ and $y=-3$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-1)^{2} & =4p(-3+4) \\\\ 1 & =4p(1) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2} & =y+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2} & =0+4 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm 2+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are $-1$  and $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-933aac48-b970-5148-a237-e6565ad9de8d" "answer-field-4b765fc4-4996-5266-90d9-3a4e2f7f9f25"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-933aac48-b970-5148-a237-e6565ad9de8d" :answer-field/id #uuid "933aac48-b970-5148-a237-e6565ad9de8d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c48e924c-701d-5314-92e8-98bc2d3981c3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c48e924c-701d-5314-92e8-98bc2d3981c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c48e924c-701d-5314-92e8-98bc2d3981c3" :answer/id #uuid "c48e924c-701d-5314-92e8-98bc2d3981c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4b765fc4-4996-5266-90d9-3a4e2f7f9f25" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b765fc4-4996-5266-90d9-3a4e2f7f9f25" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-608d4538-0b4d-5182-94b8-be0b177bf697" :answer-field/choices ["answer-608d4538-0b4d-5182-94b8-be0b177bf697"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-608d4538-0b4d-5182-94b8-be0b177bf697" :answer/id #uuid "608d4538-0b4d-5182-94b8-be0b177bf697" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-3866c2aa-e5f1-566e-84b6-7cace07a50a6" :activity/id #uuid "3866c2aa-e5f1-566e-84b6-7cace07a50a6" :activity/title "Calculating Intercepts of Parabolas" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048350 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-ec4c1f2e-ee02-534f-8b4d-4d02bf4356e6" "step-f42eea9a-325b-5c56-95b4-dc3b76529b04" "step-96d654a5-c93d-56e0-932c-bfd42b4b3f25" "step-ca9516a2-5640-5521-9384-7fc046858e73" "step-a55bc8a3-ad49-5dfc-b4d0-974e21a65508"] :activity/first-step "step-ec4c1f2e-ee02-534f-8b4d-4d02bf4356e6" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-ec4c1f2e-ee02-534f-8b4d-4d02bf4356e6" :step/id #uuid "ec4c1f2e-ee02-534f-8b4d-4d02bf4356e6" :step/content "question-f789e17e-9222-50f7-90e6-3a489f3b51f3" :step/next "step-f42eea9a-325b-5c56-95b4-dc3b76529b04" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f42eea9a-325b-5c56-95b4-dc3b76529b04" :step/id #uuid "f42eea9a-325b-5c56-95b4-dc3b76529b04" :step/content "question-f822983e-1d14-50b6-989d-68e7f1c76860" :step/next "step-96d654a5-c93d-56e0-932c-bfd42b4b3f25" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-96d654a5-c93d-56e0-932c-bfd42b4b3f25" :step/id #uuid "96d654a5-c93d-56e0-932c-bfd42b4b3f25" :step/content "question-fdc8ed74-44a5-549d-abf7-39e6c995f550" :step/next "step-ca9516a2-5640-5521-9384-7fc046858e73" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ca9516a2-5640-5521-9384-7fc046858e73" :step/id #uuid "ca9516a2-5640-5521-9384-7fc046858e73" :step/content "question-735e4f99-1ffc-57e4-b137-966d99c9aba8" :step/next "step-a55bc8a3-ad49-5dfc-b4d0-974e21a65508" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a55bc8a3-ad49-5dfc-b4d0-974e21a65508" :step/id #uuid "a55bc8a3-ad49-5dfc-b4d0-974e21a65508" :step/content 17592186441439 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078567 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d382317e-adb1-5580-86d4-be3a012ea508"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078568 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2fd9627c-83fd-577e-93d9-1dea3b352d6e" "question-bfc00702-2e19-5641-9f78-a3bfcfb36d0e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2fd9627c-83fd-577e-93d9-1dea3b352d6e" :question/id #uuid "2fd9627c-83fd-577e-93d9-1dea3b352d6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-48045" :question/problem "Given that the tangent line approximation to the function $f(x)$ at $x=3$ underestimates the function in the neighborhood of $x=3,$ which of the following must be true?" :question/worked-solution "Since the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=3$ underestimates the values of this function in the neighborhood of $x=3$, we have\n\n$$\nL(x)<f(x),\n$$\n\nfor all $x$ close to (but not equal to) $x=3.$ In other words, the line $L(x)$ must be *below* the graph of $f(x)$ near the point  $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, the function must be concave up in the neighborhood of $x=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a316d6e9-3769-5f80-845f-4a7c1ae14f3f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a316d6e9-3769-5f80-845f-4a7c1ae14f3f" :answer-field/id #uuid "a316d6e9-3769-5f80-845f-4a7c1ae14f3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7478861d-f3b8-551f-87de-db08ec6d1ea1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3920e40c-6417-5dae-af53-10980d572249" "answer-64cdcc2c-abc6-529e-a57a-d38b505a0e19" "answer-2a547162-cfa3-59b2-bf37-5f807c2a4ca9" "answer-7478861d-f3b8-551f-87de-db08ec6d1ea1" "answer-75b59e00-4955-5185-9a45-7fe9f929117b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3920e40c-6417-5dae-af53-10980d572249" :answer/id #uuid "3920e40c-6417-5dae-af53-10980d572249" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)$ has a local minimum at $x=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64cdcc2c-abc6-529e-a57a-d38b505a0e19" :answer/id #uuid "64cdcc2c-abc6-529e-a57a-d38b505a0e19" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)$ has an inflection point at $x=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a547162-cfa3-59b2-bf37-5f807c2a4ca9" :answer/id #uuid "2a547162-cfa3-59b2-bf37-5f807c2a4ca9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)$ is concave down in the neighborhood of $x=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7478861d-f3b8-551f-87de-db08ec6d1ea1" :answer/id #uuid "7478861d-f3b8-551f-87de-db08ec6d1ea1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)$ is concave up in the neighborhood of $x=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75b59e00-4955-5185-9a45-7fe9f929117b" :answer/id #uuid "75b59e00-4955-5185-9a45-7fe9f929117b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)$ is increasing in the neighborhood of $x=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d382317e-adb1-5580-86d4-be3a012ea508" :question/id #uuid "d382317e-adb1-5580-86d4-be3a012ea508" :question/math-academy-id "q-346053" :question/problem "Let $f$ be a function such that ${f}^{′}(x)=3{x}^{2}-2x$ and $f(2)=5.$ Use the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ to estimate the value of $f(2.4).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$f(2.4)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(2)+{f}^{′}(2)(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that $f(2)=5,$ and since ${f}^{′}(x)=3{x}^{2}-2x,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(2)=3(2)^{2}-2(2)=12-4=8.\n$$\n\nSo, the tangent line approximation is given by\n\n$$\nL(x)=5+8(x-2).\n$$\n\nNow, we can approximate $f(2.4)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=2.4.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2.4) & ≈L(2.4) \\\\  & =5+8(2.4-2) \\\\  & =5+8(0.4) \\\\  & =5+3.2 \\\\  & =8.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5a49ba44-a18c-572f-9889-3ebe1220fd5c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5a49ba44-a18c-572f-9889-3ebe1220fd5c" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a49ba44-a18c-572f-9889-3ebe1220fd5c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b421bb4d-d57d-58c5-91d5-941ee935054f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b421bb4d-d57d-58c5-91d5-941ee935054f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b421bb4d-d57d-58c5-91d5-941ee935054f" :answer/id #uuid "b421bb4d-d57d-58c5-91d5-941ee935054f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bfc00702-2e19-5641-9f78-a3bfcfb36d0e" :question/id #uuid "bfc00702-2e19-5641-9f78-a3bfcfb36d0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-346717" :question/problem "The graph of the function $y=f(x)$ passes through $(0,1)$ and is concave up on the interval $(-1,2).$ If ${f}^{′}(0)=1,$ estimate the value of $f(-0.3)$ using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=0$ and determine whether the approximation is an underestimate or overestimate.\n\n$\\,f(-0.3)≈$ {{field-1}} and the approximation is an {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)(x-0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph of the function passes through the point $(0,1),$ so we have $f(0)=1.$ Also, we're told that ${f}^{′}(0)=1.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =1+1(x-0) \\\\  & =1+x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can approximate $f(-0.3)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=-0.3.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-0.3) & ≈L(-0.3) \\\\  & =1+(-0.3) \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the function is concave up on the interval $(-1,2),$ the linear approximation $L(x)$ is below the graph near $x=0,$ and therefore we have an $\\text{underestimate}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-59fa50a0-4d01-5c7c-859f-4dbcf823f9f3" "answer-field-e6a25890-8790-51f7-a94b-8b42c7efdcea"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-59fa50a0-4d01-5c7c-859f-4dbcf823f9f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "59fa50a0-4d01-5c7c-859f-4dbcf823f9f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-6ecca4ab-9aea-5781-96bb-820669fd7e72" :answer-field/choices ["answer-95cb96a6-c568-5bb0-952f-972cc891d363" "answer-8500dd81-e29c-5504-be31-e4e0a9a0eb2b" "answer-6ecca4ab-9aea-5781-96bb-820669fd7e72" "answer-1be0819e-e32e-5ef6-97d4-15b2e23dacdf" "answer-ceca9693-3483-5422-9145-bd8fbfe73fda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95cb96a6-c568-5bb0-952f-972cc891d363" :answer/id #uuid "95cb96a6-c568-5bb0-952f-972cc891d363" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8500dd81-e29c-5504-b